<title>UK: Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs rise to 67 to Jan 8.</title>
<headline>Northwest Europe oil, gas rigs rise to 67 to Jan 8.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of active oil and gas rigs in operation offshore northwest Europe rose to 67 in the week ending January 8, compared with 58 rigs active in the last reported period to December 18, consultants Arthur Andersen said.</p>
<p>Seven of the new spuds were in the U.K. sector, two in the Norwegian and four in the Dutch sectors. U.K. rigs rose by five to 33, Norway rose one to 19 and the Netherlands was up three at 11 rigs. Denmark was unchanged at four.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7630</p>
</text>
